  "notes": "Validation ROC-AUC rises from 0.76331 at 10% of the training data to 0.78352 at 100%. Half the data already reaches 0.77841, and the final step from 75% to 100% adds +0.00110 against a fold-SD of 0.00595. The curve has therefore flattened: more rows of the same six-month billing snapshot would not materially help. The train-validation gap at full data is +0.03217, so the plateau is a feature-set ceiling rather than a high-variance overfit that more data would close. Together with the small tuned-versus-untuned gap from exp02, this is the evidence behind the WP18 argument that performance is limited by what a billing snapshot can observe -- it cannot see job loss, illness or income shocks -- not by model capacity."
